---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { contactEmail, contactLink } from '../site';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Parts Relay | Find car parts from a plate or VIN"
  description="Parts Relay is a web app for parts distributors and the repair shops they supply. See how plate and VIN searches, WhatsApp contacts, roles and the search queue work."
  structuredData
>
  <div class="team-page team-about">
    <section class="team-hero">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <p class="team-label">Parts Relay</p>
        <h1 tabindex="-1">About Parts Relay</h1>
        <p class="team-hero-note">
          Parts Relay is a web app for parts distributors and the repair shops they supply. Staff
          enter a registration plate or VIN and the part they need, and get back the vehicle, the
          original parts and any aftermarket matches. Workshops you add as contacts run the same
          search by WhatsApp. Parts Relay does not sell parts. The supplying branch still quotes the
          price and checks stock.
        </p>
        <div class="team-actions">
          <a class="team-btn" href={contactLink}>
            <img src="/assets/symbol-white.svg" alt="" />
            Talk to our team
          </a>
          <a class="team-btn team-secondary" href="/distributors/">
            For distributors
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="team-manifesto">
      <div>
        <section class="team-chapter">
          <p class="team-label">The people using it</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">From the service desk to the parts counter</h2>
          <p>
            A customer describes what happened to the car. The technician sees what broke. A
            distributor may have neither the car nor the repair order in front of them. Parts Relay
            gives the people answering parts enquiries a company record of the vehicle and the
            component somebody asked them to find.
          </p>
          <ol class="team-numbered">
            <li>
              <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <div>
                <strong>At the repair shop</strong>A workshop whose WhatsApp number has been added
                as a contact searches parts by sending a message. Any other number gets a reply
                asking it to contact the company.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <div>
                <strong>At the distributor</strong>Staff choose New search and enter a registration
                plate or VIN and the part needed. Searches from the counter and from WhatsApp share
                one queue.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>
        <section class="team-chapter">
          <p class="team-label">Catalogue coverage</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">Which parts appear in a search?</h2>
          <p>
            The vehicle catalogue determines the results. An entry can include the manufacturer’s
            reference, a description and an exploded view. Some entries also carry aftermarket
            cross-references.
          </p>
          <ol class="team-numbered">
            <li>
              <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Identification</strong>The counter uses the vehicle, equipment and markings
                from the old part to choose between entries.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Availability</strong>The branch supplying the part quotes its price and
                checks stock and lead time.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>
        <section class="team-chapter">
          <p class="team-label">Working together</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">A company account across shifts</h2>
          <p>
            A colleague taking over a job can reopen an earlier search, see its progress and read
            the references it found. An unresolved plate or part description stays visible to the
            team.
          </p>
          <ol class="team-numbered">
            <li>
              <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Access</strong>There are three roles. The owner manages the company and the
                team. Admins manage WhatsApp contacts and can invite or remove viewers. Viewers run
                searches and see contacts. Everyone signs in with Google or a link sent by email.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Language and country</strong>Parts Relay is available in English and
                Italian, chosen on each device. The owner sets the company’s country, and plates are
                searched in that country.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>
        <section class="team-chapter">
          <p class="team-label">Before you get in touch</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">Questions buyers ask first</h2>
          <dl class="team-qa">
            <div>
              <dt>What is Parts Relay?</dt>
              <dd>
                A web app for parts distributors and the repair shops they supply. It finds original
                and aftermarket car parts from a registration plate or VIN, lets workshops search by
                WhatsApp, and keeps every search in one company queue.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>How would my parts counter use it?</dt>
              <dd>
                Staff choose New search, pick Plate or VIN, and enter it with the part needed. The
                result shows the vehicle the catalogue identified, the original parts with their OEM
                codes and exploded views, and any aftermarket matches. Anyone on the team can reopen
                that search later from the search queue.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Can my shop request any part?</dt>
              <dd>
                A search returns what the vehicle catalogue lists for that plate or VIN. If the
                status is No category matched, try a more specific part name or its position. The
                free enquiry builder on this site is different. It writes a message for any part,
                and you send that message to your own supplier.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>How do I find out whether it covers my vehicles?</dt>
              <dd>
                Plates are searched in the country set for your company, and 33 countries are
                available: the EU and EEA countries, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United
                States. To check your own work, email two recent enquiries to
                contact@reasonandrender.com.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Does Parts Relay sell parts or quote prices?</dt>
              <dd>
                No. Results are identification guidance. The supplying branch quotes the price and
                checks stock and lead time, and fitment should be confirmed before purchase.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section class="team-chapter team-chapter-close">
          <p class="team-label">Evaluating Parts Relay</p>
          <h2 class="team-h2">Would it cover the jobs you see?</h2>
          <p>
            For a discussion about your shop, bring two recent enquiries. Pick one you answered
            easily and one that took another phone call. They give the team a way to check catalogue
            coverage against your own work and identify any follow-up you would still do with a
            supplier.
          </p>
          <p>
            Tell us which country your vehicles are registered in and which shop software you use.
            We can discuss coverage and the workflow your team needs.
          </p>
          <a class="team-contact" href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>
            Contact the Parts Relay team <span>{contactEmail}</span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactBand />
  </div>
</Layout>
